<section class="treatise-header">
  <h1 class="treatise-title">Ian Talbert</h1>
  <div class="treatise-meta">
    Mechanical Engineer &middot; Mechanism Design &middot; Kinetic Robotics
  </div>
</section>

<p class="lead">
  I am a mechanical engineer focused on the intersection of aggressive kinematic design, high-strain dynamic impacts, and pragmatic manufacturing. Whether engineering an autonomous planetary sample acquisition system with JPL-inspired microspines or designing three-pound battlebots that accelerate 800-Joule steel bars to fifteen thousand revolutions per minute, I believe true mechanical engineering is proven where theory collides violently with reality.
</p>

<p>
  Currently completing my Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering at <strong>Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology</strong>, I serve as President of the <em>Rose-Hulman Combat Robotics Team</em>. Over the past three seasons, I have designed nine scratch-built combat robots, secured back-to-back Midwest Robot Combat Association (MRCA) championships across the 1lb and 3lb divisions, and earned 29 podium placements and 13 tournament victories in 60 career bouts.
</p>

